<title>HONG KONG: Taiwan ChinaTrust gets HK banking licence.</title>
<headline>Taiwan ChinaTrust gets HK banking licence.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong Monetary Authority (HKMA) said on Monday it granted Taiwan's ChinaTrust Commercial Bank Ltd a restricted banking licence on March 4.</p>
<p>The commercial bank has been operating a representative office in Hong Kong since November, 1993 and wished to set up a restricted licence bank and participate in trading finance business, HKMA said in a statement.</p>
<p>Following the grant of a licence to ChinaTrust, the number of restricted licence banks in Hong Kong rose to 63, it added.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6369</p>
